    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d389">

                <pb facs="0757" n="647" sameAs="frus:frus1890/pg647"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wharton to Mr. Ryan.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-07-29"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 29,
                        1890</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Ryan is informed that his telegram of the 24th was not deciphered until
                    yesterday. Mr. Mizner had been telegraphed to on the 20th, instructing him to
                    tender impartial good offices, but no reply has been received from him. Action
                    upon Mexican proposition must be delayed until Mr. Mizner can be reached. Ask if
                    Mexico is in telegraphic communication with her legation in Guatemala.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
